2. HuggingFace diffusers — pipeline extensions and LTX-2 attention
================================================================================

  Source:  https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Copyright: Copyright 2024 The HuggingFace Team.

  Difflet subclasses `diffusers.<X>Pipeline` classes (FluxPipeline, WanPipeline,
  HunyuanVideoPipeline, ...) and overrides `__call__` to inject Neuron-compiled
  backbones. LTX-2 attention code in
  difflet/backends/cuda/ltx_2/official_compatibility.py adapts the upstream
  LTX2VideoTransformer3DModel attention processor under Apache License 2.0.
  Copyright 2025 The Lightricks team and The HuggingFace Team.
  The file retains the upstream license header and identifies the adaptation.

================================================================================
3. xDiT (xfuser) — design inspiration only, no code
================================================================================

  Source:  https://github.com/xdit-project/xDiT
  License: Apache License 2.0

  Difflet's overall positioning (focused DiT inference, Python API + torchrun,
  no scheduler/HTTP) and the registration decorator style are inspired by
  xDiT. No xDiT source code is copied or linked.

================================================================================
4. vLLM-Omni — LTX one-stage host numerics
================================================================================

  Source:  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-omni
  License: Apache License 2.0
  Copyright: Copyright contributors to the vLLM-Omni project.

  difflet/backends/cuda/ltx_2/official.py adapts LTX one-stage schedule,
  conditioning and BF16 sampler materialization semantics around Difflet's
  transformer. official_compatibility.py also adapts its BF16 rotary
  materialization order. These files do not depend on the vLLM-Omni runtime.
